  "final_text": "I looked up both items with read-only API calls and changed nothing.\n\n1. **Panels:** The 'Site health' dashboard has 2 panels. Both are charts: \"Requests over time\", a line chart of request count, and \"Requests by response code\", a bar chart of the top 10 response codes. It has no pinned panels, and the Dashboards API and the raw saved object both show the same 2.\n2. **Rule name:** The rule is called **Server errors**. It's the only alert rule in Kibana. It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that matches any `response.keyword` starting with \"5\".\n3. **Check interval:** It runs every **1m**. Each run looks back over the last 5 minutes and fires if it finds more than 10 matching requests. The 5-minute look-back is separate from how often the rule runs.\n4. **Enabled:** **No**, the rule is disabled, so it isn't running right now.\n\nPANELS: 2\nRULE_NAME: Server errors\nINTERVAL: 1m\nENABLED: no",
